{"id":"bbbedaecb57ada11","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-pure-projective.md","title":"Pure Projective Module","display":"df-pure-projective — Pure Projective Module","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-pure-projective","aliases":["58-df-pure-projective"],"display":"df-pure-projective — Pure Projective Module","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-module.md]]","[[../batch05/58-df-surjective.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-zfc-algebra2-module-homomorphism.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-pure-projective"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-pure-projective</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-pure-projective — Pure Projective Module"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ef3a5dd6825f0373\" href=\"?note=ef3a5dd6825f0373\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-module.md\">../batch13/58-df-module.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"9f8cb046321ba311\" href=\"?note=9f8cb046321ba311\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-surjective.md\">../batch05/58-df-surjective.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"25e593b1b8714c23\" href=\"?note=25e593b1b8714c23\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-zfc-algebra2-module-homomorphism.md\">../batch16/58-df-zfc-algebra2-module-homomorphism.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span> (ring) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,P,N,F\">\\(M,P,N,F\\)</span> (left <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span>-modules)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Module}\">\\(\\operatorname{Module}\\)</span> (carrier-level module predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ef3a5dd6825f0373\" href=\"?note=ef3a5dd6825f0373\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-module.md\">../batch13/58-df-module.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ModuleHomomorphism}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ModuleHomomorphism}_S\\)</span> (module-homomorphism predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"25e593b1b8714c23\" href=\"?note=25e593b1b8714c23\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-zfc-algebra2-module-homomorphism.md\">../batch16/58-df-zfc-algebra2-module-homomorphism.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Surjective}\">\\(\\mathrm{Surjective}\\)</span> (surjectivity predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FinitelyPresentedModule}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{FinitelyPresentedModule}_S\\)</span> (finite-presentation predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PureEpimorphism}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{PureEpimorphism}_S\\)</span> (pure-epimorphism predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PureProjective}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{PureProjective}_S\\)</span> (pure-projective predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pure\\text{-}projective\\text{-}hom} \\vdash \\operatorname{Hom}_R(M,N)\\coloneqq\\{f\\in N^M:\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ModuleHomomorphism}_S(f,M,N,R)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pure\\text{-}projective\\text{-}hom} \\vdash \\operatorname{Hom}_R(M,N)\\coloneqq\\{f\\in N^M:\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ModuleHomomorphism}_S(f,M,N,R)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pure\\text{-}projective\\text{-}finite\\text{-}presentation} \\vdash \\operatorname{FinitelyPresentedModule}_S(F,R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Module}(F,R)\\land\\exists m,n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists A\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(R^m,R^n)\\;\\exists q\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(R^n,F)\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Surjective}(q,R^n,F)\\land\\ker(q)=\\operatorname{ran}(A)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pure\\text{-}projective\\text{-}finite\\text{-}presentation} \\vdash \\operatorname{FinitelyPresentedModule}_S(F,R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Module}(F,R)\\land\\exists m,n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists A\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(R^m,R^n)\\;\\exists q\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(R^n,F)\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Surjective}(q,R^n,F)\\land\\ker(q)=\\operatorname{ran}(A)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pure\\text{-}projective\\text{-}epimorphism} \\vdash \\operatorname{PureEpimorphism}_S(\\pi,P,N,R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Module}(P,R)\\land\\operatorname{Module}(N,R)\\land\\pi\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(P,N)\\land\\mathrm{Surjective}(\\pi,P,N)\\land\\forall F\\;\\left(\\operatorname{FinitelyPresentedModule}_S(F,R)\\to\\forall h\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(F,N)\\;\\exists\\widetilde h\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(F,P)\\;(\\pi\\circ\\widetilde h=h)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pure\\text{-}projective\\text{-}epimorphism} \\vdash \\operatorname{PureEpimorphism}_S(\\pi,P,N,R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Module}(P,R)\\land\\operatorname{Module}(N,R)\\land\\pi\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(P,N)\\land\\mathrm{Surjective}(\\pi,P,N)\\land\\forall F\\;\\left(\\operatorname{FinitelyPresentedModule}_S(F,R)\\to\\forall h\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(F,N)\\;\\exists\\widetilde h\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(F,P)\\;(\\pi\\circ\\widetilde h=h)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pure\\text{-}projective} \\vdash \\operatorname{PureProjective}_S(M,R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Module}(M,R)\\land\\forall P,N,\\pi\\;\\left(\\operatorname{PureEpimorphism}_S(\\pi,P,N,R)\\to\\forall h\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(M,N)\\;\\exists\\widetilde h\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(M,P)\\;(\\pi\\circ\\widetilde h=h)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}pure\\text{-}projective} \\vdash \\operatorname{PureProjective}_S(M,R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Module}(M,R)\\land\\forall P,N,\\pi\\;\\left(\\operatorname{PureEpimorphism}_S(\\pi,P,N,R)\\to\\forall h\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(M,N)\\;\\exists\\widetilde h\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_R(M,P)\\;(\\pi\\circ\\widetilde h=h)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Pure projectivity is stated by its lifting property against pure epimorphisms. Module-homomorphism sets and finite presentations are grounded in the exact carrier-level module and module-homomorphism predicates.</li>\n<li>The implication “projective implies pure projective” is a downstream theorem and has been removed.</li>\n<li>Equivalently, a pure-projective module is a direct summand of a direct sum of finitely presented modules.</li>\n<li>Countably presented pure projective modules are projective over Noetherian rings.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-module.md","status":"resolved","id":"ef3a5dd6825f0373","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-module.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-surjective.md","status"